; dec-branch-loop-deep --- deep nested-loop probe for §5.21 / §6 /
; §5.19 (DEC / BRANCH_ON / LOAD_LOOP) and the BRANCH_ON signed
; 10-bit offset reach (§5.11).
;
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
; What this probe locks
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; Outer loop counter: R5, primed to 255 (raw LOAD_IMM since the
; LOAD_LOOP sugar only targets R6 per §5.18).
; Inner loop counter: R6, primed to 255 via LOAD_LOOP sugar.
;
; Each outer iteration:
;   - Reload R6 to 255 (via LOAD_LOOP).
;   - Inner body: 8 EMIT_BIT_IMM (one byte's worth of dominant pulses)
;     + DEC R6 + BRANCH_ON NOT_REG_ZERO.
;   - After the inner loop exits (R6 == 0), DEC R5 + BRANCH_ON
;     NOT_REG_ZERO back to the outer-body top.
;
; Total wire activity: 255 outer × 255 inner × 8 bits = 520,200
; SDA pulses. The bytecode itself is tiny because both loops live
; entirely in registers --- this is the point of v0.2's two-register
; loop convention.
;
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
; BRANCH_ON reach verification
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; Per §5.11 BRANCH_ON encodes a signed 10-bit PC-offset at [12:3],
; i.e. branches can reach -512..+511 instructions from `branch_pc + 1`.
; Loop bodies in this program are intentionally compact:
;
;   Inner body span (from `inner_top` to the inner BRANCH_ON):
;     8 EMIT_BIT_IMM + DEC + BRANCH_ON = 10 instructions
;     → back-edge offset = -10 (well within ±511)
;
;   Outer body span (from `outer_top` to the outer BRANCH_ON):
;     1 LOAD_LOOP + 10 inner-body insns + DEC + BRANCH_ON = 13
;     → back-edge offset = -13 (well within ±511)
;
; If a future codegen pass inflates the inner body past 512
; instructions, the assembler MUST raise E-RNG-001 (BRANCH_ON
; offset out of signed 10-bit range). This fixture is the
; positive case: comfortably small back-edges that MUST encode
; without complaint.
;
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
; v0.2 spelling
; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; DEC + BRANCH_ON {REG_ZERO|NOT_REG_ZERO} replaces the v0 fused
; DEC_BRANCH. Back-to-back is hazard-free per §14 (no LINT-001).
; The two-counter convention is R6 inner (LOAD_LOOP sugar target) /
; R5 outer (raw LOAD_IMM). Higher-numbered Rx (R0..R4) remain
; unused here and are general-purpose per §8.
;
; EMIT_BIT_IMM uses i2c bus mode just to give it a meaningful
; vocabulary; this is not a real I2C transaction.

        LOAD_TIMING       reg=0, divider=59
        SET_BUS_MODE      i2c
        SET_ROLE          controller

        LOAD_IMM          R5, 255           ; outer counter
outer_top:
        LOAD_LOOP         255               ; inner counter via R6 sugar
inner_top:
        EMIT_BIT_IMM      tx=dominant
        EMIT_BIT_IMM      tx=dominant
        EMIT_BIT_IMM      tx=dominant
        EMIT_BIT_IMM      tx=dominant
        EMIT_BIT_IMM      tx=dominant
        EMIT_BIT_IMM      tx=dominant
        EMIT_BIT_IMM      tx=dominant
        EMIT_BIT_IMM      tx=dominant
        DEC               R6
        BRANCH_ON         NOT_REG_ZERO, inner_top

        DEC               R5
        BRANCH_ON         NOT_REG_ZERO, outer_top

        HALT              status=0
